🔤 Day 19: String Reverser + Case Converter Tool

📌 Project Overview

This project is a String Reverser + Case Converter Tool built using Python.
The program asks the user to enter a string and provides a menu of different string operations:

🔄 Reverse the string
🔠 Convert to UPPERCASE
🔡 Convert to lowercase
📝 Convert to Title Case
🔃 Swap Case
🚪 Exit

After performing an operation, the program also counts the uppercase and lowercase letters in the resulting string.
This project builds on the string concepts learned in Days 16–18.



✨ Features

🔄 1. Reverse the String

The program uses string slicing:

ste0 = ste[::-1]

Example:

Hello World

becomes:

dlroW olleH


🔠 2. Convert to UPPERCASE

The program uses:

ste0 = ste.upper()

Example:

Hello World

becomes:

HELLO WORLD


🔡 3. Convert to lowercase

The program uses:

ste0 = ste.lower()

Example:

Hello World

becomes:

hello world


📝 4. Convert to Title Case

The program uses:

ste0 = ste.title()

Example:

hello world

becomes:

Hello World

Each word starts with an uppercase letter.


🔃 5. Swap Case

The program uses:

ste0 = ste.swapcase()

Example:

Hello World

becomes:

hELLO wORLD

Uppercase letters become lowercase, and lowercase letters become uppercase.


🚪 6. Exit

The user can select:

6. Exit

and the program stops.

There is also a q/Q option when entering the string:

if ste == "q" or ste == "Q":


🎁 Bonus Features

🔤 Count Uppercase Letters

You implemented the second bonus feature:

up_c = 0

for char in ste0:
    if char.isupper():
        up_c += 1

The program counts every uppercase letter in the resulting string.



🔡 Count Lowercase Letters

Similarly:

lw_c = 0

for char in ste0:
    if char.islower():
        lw_c += 1

This counts every lowercase letter.



🔄 New String Each Time

You also implemented the first bonus in a slightly different way.

The program asks for a new string at the beginning of every while loop:

while True:
    ste = input("Enter a string or (press q to Quit): ")

So after an operation finishes, the program returns to the beginning and allows another string to be entered.



