🧠 String Methods Learned

Day 19 introduces several useful Python string methods.

.upper()
text.upper()

Converts letters to uppercase.

hello → HELLO
.lower()
text.lower()

Converts letters to lowercase.

HELLO → hello
.title()
text.title()

Capitalizes the beginning of each word.

hello world → Hello World
.swapcase()
text.swapcase()

Flips the case of each letter.

Hello World → hELLO wORLD
[::-1]

You learned this in Day 16.

text[::-1]

reverses the string.

Hello → olleH


🔍 .isupper() and .islower()

Your bonus introduces two more useful string methods.

.isupper()
char.isupper()

asks:

"Is this character uppercase?"

Example:

A → True
a → False
.islower()
char.islower()

asks:

"Is this character lowercase?"

Example:

a → True
A → False


👶 Simple Way to Understand the Program

Imagine you give Python a sentence:

Hello World

Then Python gives you a toolbox:

┌─────────────────────────┐
│     STRING TOOLBOX      │
├─────────────────────────┤
│ 1 → Reverse             │
│ 2 → UPPERCASE           │
│ 3 → lowercase           │
│ 4 → Title Case          │
│ 5 → Swap Case           │
│ 6 → Exit                │
└─────────────────────────┘

You choose a tool, Python changes the string, and then the program counts its uppercase and lowercase letters.



